Files created:
- Cargo.toml - depends on aes = "0.8" for AES-256-ECB (replacing OpenSSL)
- src/main.rs - KAT transcript logic (SHA2_TR mode using SHA-512)
- src/params.rs - all SPHINCS+ sha2-256s constants
- src/context.rs - SpxCtx struct with SHA-256/512 seeded states
- src/sha2.rs - full SHA-256/SHA-512 implementation (incremental API), MGF1, seed_state
- src/address.rs - address manipulation (byte-level access to [u32; 8])
- src/hash.rs - prf_addr, gen_message_random (HMAC-SHA-512), hash_message
- src/thash.rs - tweakable hash (SHA-256 for 1 block, SHA-512 for >1 blocks)
- src/utils.rs - compute_root (Merkle auth path verification)
- src/wots.rs - WOTS+ chain generation, base_w, chain_lengths, wots_pk_from_sig
- src/wotsx1.rs - wots_gen_leafx1 (WOTS key/sig generation)
- src/fors.rs - FORS sign/verify, treehash for both FORS and WOTS
- src/merkle.rs - merkle_sign, merkle_gen_root
- src/sign.rs - top-level crypto_sign_keypair, crypto_sign, crypto_sign_open
- src/rng.rs - AES-256-CTR-DRBG (deterministic RNG matching the C rng.c)

Key design decisions:
- Used unsafe only for the global DRBG state (matching C's global DRBG_ctx)
- Borrow checker conflicts resolved with temporary copies (e.g., thash on overlapping buffer slices)
- The aes crate replaces OpenSSL's EVP_aes_256_ecb for the DRBG
